---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
---

<StaticPage 
  title="About Us - OnSciCalc"
  description="Learn about OnSciCalc, the best free online scientific calculator for students, engineers, and professionals. Discover our mission to make math accessible."
  canonical="https://onscicalc.com/about-us"
>

  <article class="prose-custom">
    <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-ink font-geist tracking-tight mb-2">About Us</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink/50 font-geist mb-8">Making mathematics accessible for everyone.</p>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70 font-geist">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Our Mission</h2>
        <p>
          OnSciCalc was built with a simple mission: to provide a powerful, free, and accessible scientific calculator that anyone can use — without downloads, without accounts, and without limitations. We believe that access to reliable mathematical tools should never be a barrier to learning or professional work.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">What We Offer</h2>
        <p>
          Our online scientific calculator combines the functionality of dedicated hardware calculators — like the Casio fx-991es and Texas Instruments models — with the convenience of modern web technology. Here's what makes OnSciCalc stand out:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 mt-3">
          <li><strong>Comprehensive Scientific Functions</strong> — Trigonometric functions (sin, cos, tan and their inverses), logarithms, exponents, square roots, cube roots, factorials, and more.</li>
          <li><strong>Fraction Support</strong> — Perform fraction calculations directly in the calculator interface.</li>
          <li><strong>Dual Mode</strong> — Switch between Beginner and Advanced modes based on your skill level and needs.</li>
          <li><strong>DEG/RAD Toggle</strong> — Easily switch between degree and radian angle modes for trigonometric calculations.</li>
          <li><strong>AI-Powered Suggestions</strong> — Get intelligent expression suggestions as you type, reducing syntax errors and speeding up your workflow.</li>
          <li><strong>Calculation History</strong> — Review and reuse previous calculations with the built-in history panel.</li>
          <li><strong>Keyboard Shortcuts</strong> — Power users can type expressions directly using keyboard shortcuts for maximum speed.</li>
          <li><strong>Dark & Light Themes</strong> — Comfortable viewing in any lighting condition with automatic theme persistence.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Who We're For</h2>
        <p>OnSciCalc is designed for a wide range of users:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 mt-3">
          <li><strong>Students</strong> — From high school algebra to university calculus, OnSciCalc supports the mathematical operations you need for coursework.</li>
          <li><strong>Engineers</strong> — Electrical, mechanical, civil, and software engineers can rely on our calculator for quick computations involving complex numbers, matrices, and statistical functions.</li>
          <li><strong>Scientists</strong> — Researchers and lab professionals can perform rapid calculations with scientific notation and precision functions.</li>
          <li><strong>Professionals</strong> — Anyone who needs fast, reliable mathematical computations in their daily work.</li>
          <li><strong>Educators</strong> — Teachers and tutors can use OnSciCalc as a teaching tool in classrooms and online sessions.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Built with Modern Technology</h2>
        <p>
          OnSciCalc is built using cutting-edge web technologies including Astro, Tailwind CSS, and TypeScript. Our calculator runs entirely in your browser — all computations happen locally on your device, ensuring your data stays private and calculations are instant.
        </p>
        <p>
          We test and optimize our calculator across all modern browsers including Chrome, Firefox, Safari, and Edge, and ensure it works flawlessly on desktop, tablet, and mobile devices.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Our Commitment</h2>
        <p>
          We are committed to keeping OnSciCalc free, ad-free (or minimally monetized), and continuously improving. We welcome feedback from our users and actively incorporate feature requests and bug reports into our development roadmap.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you have suggestions, found a bug, or just want to say hello, don't hesitate to reach out through our <a href="/contact-us" class="text-brand-link hover:underline">Contact Us</a> page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Get Started</h2>
        <p>
          Ready to calculate? Head back to our <a href="/" class="text-brand-link hover:underline">calculator</a> and start computing.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>

</StaticPage>
